Date: Sun, 29 Nov 2026 05:23:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] The 3-D split's seam gate tests the closure of the
 patch's cell star

split_along_label_3d refuses when any point in the closure of a cell with a
vertex on the patch is shared; split_fault's gate (_fault_labels_touch_seam)
tested only the fault facets and the points below them, the 2-D rule. So at
np 3 a patch whose star reached the seam off the facets was not
repartitioned, and the split refused it (ptest_0848). One helper,
_patch_star_touches_seam, now holds the refusal's test; the refusal calls it,
and the gate calls it in 3-D, still reduced over every rank. The repartition
it triggers (partition_addon with one layer, or _gather_regions with one
layer on the extrude path) already makes every point of a star cell
unshared. 2-D is unchanged.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
